From ca95740de09eb55b8476e16eb857ae07a64623da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:07:36 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(slot): cut the round ends of a slot wider than the
 tool

A row of a wide Slot touches each round end only at its end point. The
tool did not follow the arc between two row ends and left up to 0.86 mm
on the wall (10 mm slot, 6 mm tool), and verify passed it.

After the rows, each level now runs one lap of the cutter-centre stadium
from the last row's end: two straight sides and two half circles, each
half circle as two quarter arcs. The lap is counterclockwise under climb
and clockwise otherwise. A full-width slot (h = 0) is unchanged.

Goldens: slot_wide_channel_rows (CL and each NC dialect) gain the six lap
moves for each level; the catalog case 2d/slots is rebuilt.

Fixes #2906

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
