From 35020f6cc294c3b6266be720b3c9d2b178c970f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 01:19:24 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(slot): split the wall lap at each row end so no row
 join crosses it

The verifier's crossing law flattens an arc into chords inside its circle. A row join ends exactly on the circle, so it crossed the flattened quarter arcs of the lap, and the post of each wide slot was held (8 app suites). Each cap is now split at every row end and at its tip. The rows and the lap compute a row end with one function (cap_point), so they share each vertex to the bit, and the law reads a touch.

Tests: slot_round_ends checks the crossing law and a slot whose rows are off the cap tips. Expected-change updates: operations and example_catalog count only descending arcs as an orbit, or the lap arcs; clearance_in_stock: the slot's traverse between levels now rides over its own channel and is acquitted, and the post stays held by the first traverse and the rapid into the stock.

Refs #2906

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
